# 15. 🎯 Make Time vs. Manage Time

This distinction is powerful.

Traditional productivity asks:

> **"How can I manage all my time?"**

*Make Time* asks:

> **"What do I want to make time for?"**

That's a completely different mindset.

Imagine you say:

> "I don't have time for DSA."

Instead of accepting that statement, investigate:

```text
24 hours
 ↓
Sleep
 ↓
College
 ↓
Travel
 ↓
Phone
 ↓
YouTube
 ↓
WhatsApp
 ↓
Random tasks
 ↓
Remaining time
```

Maybe the issue isn't literally a lack of time.

Maybe time is being **claimed by default**.

